<h1 id="a-preface">A preface</h1>
    {{> writing_byline_dateline author="Arjun Satarkar" pub_date=pub_date}}
<p>It has been traditional for the first post made to a blog to express
the author’s intentions, hopes, and reasons for beginning one. Whatever
I may call this, which if my intent is borne out will grow to be a
collection of writing, it shares enough characteristics with blogs to
adhere to the same convention. So:</p>
<h2 id="why">Why?</h2>
<p>Self-centered reasons. Writing original text is a hubristic
endeavour.</p>
<p>There is not a single specific impetus for this; I don’t have a
unitary message I want to get out there. There <em>are</em> many
<em>individual</em> things I’d like to write, and I would also like to
be the sort of person who in fact writes them.</p>
<p>Humans are no longer the only entities that can write in human
languages. Current AI is not very good at the craft of writing, and its
output can typically be detected, but maybe that will not be true
forever. Maybe I am motivated to start <em>actually writing</em> now in particular because of some sense
of impending threat.</p>
<p>Really, though, I think I have at least abstractly wanted to write
since before any of that happened, and so this is me doing that.</p>
<p>As such:</p>
<h2 id="who-how">Who? How?</h2>
<p>Everything here is and will be written by me, the named author at the
top, excepting quotations, which will be marked and delimited according
to convention. (If I at some point write with a coauthor, they will also
be named at the top of the relevant pages.) I will not ask artificial
intelligence to edit my writing or provide advice. That would entirely
defeat the purpose.</p>
<p>Rather than describe myself, I hope that my writing will stand as an
expression of me. There is also <a href="https://arjunsatarkar.net/">a
home page</a>.</p>
<h2 id="for-whom"><small>For</small> Whom?</h2>
<p>I hope things I write will be read by people who find them
interesting.</p>
<h2 id="what">What?</h2>
<p>I am interested in, and will write about: • systems of various sorts
<small>(computer, legal)</small>, • language <small>(interesting
grammatical features, etymology, learning Japanese)</small>, • fiction
<small>(novels, Japanese animation, hypertext media, and so
forth)</small>, and probably other things.</p>
    </article>
